<title>RUSSIA: Russia Nizhnetagilsk soars on ADR news.</title>
<headline>Russia Nizhnetagilsk soars on ADR news.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Russia's Nizhnetagilsk steel maker rose 18 percent in thin trade on Wednesday afternoon after the company said it planned to issue American Depositary Receipts to allow trade on foreign exchanges.</p>
<p>Nizhnetagilsk had soared to $0.144 at 1258 GMT on the Russian Trading System from its Tuesday close of $0.122 on reported volume of 400,000 shares.</p>
<p>A Nizhnetagilsk official said the company planned to issue Level One ADRs or privately placed 144-A ADRs as soon as November.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
